    { title: "Measure the waiting work", paragraphs: ["A remote support lane becomes teachable when its evidence is visible. In donation processing coordination, a Filipino team member should be able to identify the source, perform the defined check, and state the unresolved question without pretending to own the final decision. Close each review with a dated decision record: item or batch, evidence considered, question asked, owner response, affected example, and next review date. If the rule changes, identify records that may need another look. If it does not change, preserve the explanation for the next worker. That operating history turns donation processing coordination into a dependable support lane without transferring authority away from the client."] }
